# Expo Go only (no dev builds)

The user **cannot run `expo run:ios` / EAS builds right now**. All work must run in **Expo Go**.

## Do

- Prefer **JS-only** solutions and Expo Go–supported APIs (`expo-av`, `expo-image-picker`, etc.).
- **Lazy-import** custom native modules (`@kingstinct/react-native-healthkit`, `@react-native-google-signin/google-signin`, `react-native-nitro-modules`) — never top-level import in files loaded at startup.
- Guard native features with `isExpoGo()` from `src/utils/isExpoGo.js` and show a clear message or guest/skip fallback.
- Skip push token registration in Expo Go (`useClarityData`).

## Do not

- Add new native modules or `app.json` plugins that require a rebuild.
- Tell the user to run a dev build as the only fix — offer Expo Go–compatible alternatives first.
- Import HealthKit, Google Sign-In, or Nitro packages at module scope in `App.js` or hooks used on launch.

## Expo Go limitations (graceful degradation)

